From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ivo Nunes <ivo@nunes.uk>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 19:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Metal: keep slices of multisampled textures multisampled

texture_create_shared_from_slice() always asked Metal for a plain 2D
(or 2D array) view. Forward+ resolves MSAA in multiview through a view
of one layer of the multisampled colour array, and Metal refuses a
non-multisampled view of multisampled memory, so XR with MSAA aborted
the renderer on Metal. A slice of a multisampled texture is now a
TextureType2DMultisample (or 2DMultisampleArray) view.

Test: an XR viewport with two views and MSAA 2x or 4x on Metal renders
instead of aborting.

Upstream: to propose.
---
diff --git a/godot/drivers/metal/rendering_device_driver_metal.cpp b/godot/drivers/metal/rendering_device_driver_metal.cpp
index 1d5efcb..ac1306c 100644
--- a/godot/drivers/metal/rendering_device_driver_metal.cpp
+++ b/godot/drivers/metal/rendering_device_driver_metal.cpp
@@ -536,9 +536,11 @@ RDD::TextureID RenderingDeviceDriverMetal::texture_create_shared_from_slice(Text
 	};
 
 	MTL::TextureType textureType = VIEW_TYPES[src_texture->textureType()];
+	// A view of multisampled layers must stay multisampled: Metal refuses a plain 2D view of them.
+	const bool multisampled = src_texture->textureType() == MTL::TextureType2DMultisample || src_texture->textureType() == MTL::TextureType2DMultisampleArray;
 	switch (p_slice_type) {
 		case TEXTURE_SLICE_2D: {
-			textureType = MTL::TextureType2D;
+			textureType = multisampled ? MTL::TextureType2DMultisample : MTL::TextureType2D;
 		} break;
 		case TEXTURE_SLICE_3D: {
 			textureType = MTL::TextureType3D;
@@ -547,7 +549,7 @@ RDD::TextureID RenderingDeviceDriverMetal::texture_create_shared_from_slice(Text
 			textureType = MTL::TextureTypeCube;
 		} break;
 		case TEXTURE_SLICE_2D_ARRAY: {
-			textureType = MTL::TextureType2DArray;
+			textureType = multisampled ? MTL::TextureType2DMultisampleArray : MTL::TextureType2DArray;
 		} break;
 		case TEXTURE_SLICE_MAX: {
 			ERR_FAIL_V_MSG(TextureID(), "Invalid texture slice type");
